    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Issues and Fixes\n\n**1. Governance Module - Missing Named Export**\n   - **Problem**: The test imported `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export\n   - **Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` in `src/finetune/index.js`\n\n**2. Evaluation - Toxicity Metric Signature Mismatch**\n   - **Problem**: `toxicityMetric` was being called with `(outputs, references)` but expected `(outputs, bannedTerms)`, causing the references array to be misinterpreted as banned terms\n   - **Fix**: Updated the function signature to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to match the calling pattern while maintaining the default banned terms behavior\n\nAll 28 tests now pass across 8 test files. The public API remains unchanged with all existing exports preserved.",
